1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:06,453
SUTRA onboards the Government provided cameras automatically from the challenge portal's own catalogue.

2
00:00:06,453 --> 00:00:15,326
Thirty live feeds across five departments, a mix of H two six four and H two six five, at different resolutions.

3
00:00:15,326 --> 00:00:21,508
They are pulled over authenticated R T S P, with credentials injected at connection time.

4
00:00:21,508 --> 00:00:28,654
The credentials are never written into the registry, never logged, and never stored with the camera record.

5
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:31,485
Live viewing of the Government feeds.

6
00:00:31,485 --> 00:00:39,026
These are the portal's cameras — Junagadh, Gir Somnath, Ahmedabad — decoding right now on this machine.

7
00:00:39,026 --> 00:00:42,368
We measured the portal before designing for it.

8
00:00:42,368 --> 00:00:49,524
It rations delivery to about five megabits per second per client, whether you open ten connections or twenty.

9
00:00:49,524 --> 00:00:52,382
That is three to four real time streams.

10
00:00:52,382 --> 00:01:00,559
So the scheduler rotates all thirty cameras through the slots available, rather than opening thirty connections that would all starve.

11
00:01:00,650 --> 00:01:04,513
Number plate recognition running on the Government feeds.

12
00:01:04,513 --> 00:01:13,928
These are today's reads from the Junagadh and Gir Somnath cameras, each one with the camera it came from, a timestamp, and the confidence of the read.

13
00:01:13,928 --> 00:01:16,754
That confidence column is deliberate.

14
00:01:16,754 --> 00:01:20,871
These are plates fifty to ninety pixels tall on a live street.

15
00:01:20,871 --> 00:01:24,920
Reads above about zero point nine five are reliable.

16
00:01:24,920 --> 00:01:27,638
Below that, characters can be wrong.

17
00:01:27,638 --> 00:01:33,521
Publishing the number without the confidence would invite you to treat every row as a fact.

18
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:35,631
Every read is evidenced.

19
00:01:35,631 --> 00:01:43,185
This is the actual crop the recognition ran on, kept alongside the detection, so any read can be checked by a human.

20
00:01:43,185 --> 00:01:48,226
That is the minimum bar for anything that might support an investigation.

21
00:01:48,340 --> 00:01:53,493
And this is the required output report, straight from the Government feeds.

22
00:01:53,493 --> 00:02:04,961
Eighty two plate reads over a two hour run, fifty one distinct registration numbers, each with U T C and I S T timestamps and a path to its evidence image.

23
00:02:05,070 --> 00:02:12,506
Completing the Model One foundation: a layered coverage map by department, camera type and status.

24
00:02:12,506 --> 00:02:17,968
District level gap analysis showing thin coverage and ageing infrastructure.

25
00:02:17,968 --> 00:02:25,155
And a full metadata audit trail — every onboarding, export and watchlist change recorded against a user.

26
00:02:25,155 --> 00:02:30,644
The hosted platform, the source code and this report are all linked in the submission.
